There are four input files for the Fy(IVP3) family of parametrizations:

for005.FyIVP3ZR_nonat   zero-range Fy(IVP3) with standard HFB iteration
for005.FyIVP3ZR_nat     zero-range Fy(IVP3) with sub-iterations in 'HFB_natural'
for005.FyIVP3FR_nonat   finite-range Fy(IVP3) with standard HFB iteration
for005.FyIVP3FR_nat     finite-range Fy(IVP3) with sub-iterations in 'HFB_natural'

The termination criterion is in all cases 'errenr=1D-11'. This guarantees for 158Yb
radii to at least four digits and energies to at least five digits. 

The version with sub-iterations in 'HFB_natural' uses a bit longer for one step,
but converges faster. It is the preferable.

For large-scale scans, one may sacrifice a bit of precision and use larger 'errenr'.


The choice of convergence parameters, in particular 'x0inv', may be
further explored. Larger 'x0inv' gives faster convergence, but
unhances the danger of being trapped in HFB isomers. More than
'x0inv=0.2' is not recommended.